---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const SIM_URL = 'https://sim.failurefirst.ai';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="SimLab — Failure-First Embodied AI"
  description="SimLab is Failure-First's instrument for replaying causal evidence from embodied AI experiments: a small shortlist of specimens, each shown as record, cause, consequence and receipt. Rendering is derived visualisation, never primary evidence."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'SimLab' }]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAILURE-FIRST &middot; AN INSTRUMENT, NOT A DEMO &middot; REPLAY</p>
    <h1>SimLab</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      SimLab is where our experiments are watched. Each specimen is a recorded run
      you can replay: what the model was told, what it chose, what the world did
      back, and what the receipt says the run actually establishes. The subject is
      the causal boundary between a decision and its consequence &mdash; not robots
      moving.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href={SIM_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Open SimLab <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Three specimen doors, one at a time</h2>
      <p>
        A cold visit stages nothing; you are shown a short list rather than an
        archive. <strong>OUTSIDE THE PETRI DISH</strong> &mdash; a model given an
        embodied objective with no world wired up behind it tried to build the
        missing world out of the tools it actually had. <strong>THE CONDUCTOR</strong>
        &mdash; one sung instruction switched a habitat's heat off; the recovery
        instruction arrived after the body had moved, recorded exposure crossed an
        injury threshold, and the water kept rising. <strong>IT DID EXACTLY WHAT I
        SAID</strong> &mdash; an accepted stop command dropped a standing robot and
        kept it down for eleven seconds.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Every specimen says what it does not prove</h2>
      <p>
        A specimen earns a front door because the causal work is legible in it,
        never because something moves attractively. Where the apparatus could not
        test the claim the run appears to make, the door retracts it in writing
        &mdash; <em>NOT TESTED</em> rather than a quiet omission &mdash; and
        reconstructed articulation is labelled as reconstructed rather than
        measured. Recordings keep their provenance: classification, source run,
        byte counts and hashes.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>The archive is behind the doors</h2>
      <p>
        Controls, nulls, oddities and the full historical corpus are deliberately
        one click away rather than the opening screen. That is where the forensic
        console lives: recorded events, model calls, world state, the radio traffic
        between robots, and the falsifier that ran. A presentation layer never gets
        to promote itself into evidence.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Rendering is derived, and says so</h2>
      <p>
        Every pixel derives from a finalized, hash-addressed recording. Replayed
        joint articulation is marked <code>RECONSTRUCTED ARTICULATION</code> with its
        limitation in the provenance block. A camera mounted on the recorded pose is
        <code>DERIVED_VIEW</code>, never sensor imagery, because none was captured.
        Channels a trace does not carry render <code>UNAVAILABLE</code> instead of
        invented values.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>UTOPIA / DYSTOPIA is a light switch</h2>
      <p>
        A presentation-only world switch: the same recorded evidence renders as a
        bright robotics-institute laboratory or a dark industrial one. Camera
        geometry, timestamps, and verdicts are provably unaffected &mdash; only
        pixels change.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Built for scrutiny</h2>
      <p>
        Deterministic deep links (<code>?specimen=&hellip;&amp;t=&hellip;&amp;paused</code>),
        an independent release oracle that observes candidate and production builds
        separately, strict schema validation on every recording, and official Unitree
        URDF/mesh assets pinned to an exact upstream commit with a SHA-256
        manifest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="footnote">
    Source: <code>apps/simviz/</code> in the research repository. Rendering is
    <code>DERIVED_VISUALISATION</code> &mdash; it never alters or implies
    changes to a recorded trajectory.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--fg-muted, #7a8292);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg, #e8ecf2);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
    margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--accent-primary, #00d2ff);
    color: #050810;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-bottom: none;
    transition: transform 150ms ease, box-shadow 150ms ease;
  }
  .cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.25);
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(232, 236, 242, 0.08));
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-card, #0f1621);
  }
  .card h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg, #e8ecf2);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .card code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #00d2ff);
  }

  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted, #7a8292);
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(232, 236, 242, 0.08));
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .footnote code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
  }
</style>
